A||N||12||FieroKyle||Sprint Manifold||||4||
Z||000000||FieroKyle||11-27-2001||10:47 PM||||I am considering putting these on, but has the hefty pricetag of around $500. What I am asking is really worth the money for these? They are supposed to get around 20 hp more, but I have talked to people before and they can't feel any difference, just that it sounds cooler. I just have a stock 2.8, only this is it has not Cat Con. I am putting a new exhaust on the car so figured my as well may be do the manifolds.<P>Also what does a good exhaust run if ya put it on yourself? Thanks for any answers.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierokylesig_1.gif">      <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||4
Z||000001||Raydar||11-27-2001||10:57 PM||||I've heard from many people thaat the Sprint manifolds are worth 4-8 HP. Pretty much the same as porting your stock exhaust manifolds. The Sprints just look cooler.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroKyle||11-27-2001||11:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B>I've heard from many people thaat the Sprint manifolds are worth 4-8 HP. Pretty much the same as porting your stock exhaust manifolds. The Sprints just look cooler.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not interested in porting.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||ThatRickGuy||11-27-2001||11:00 PM||||I'm using ported manifolds, no cat and a free flowing stealess steal exhaust system, definately a bump up from stock, and the whole set up cost less then just those sprint manifolds. All in all, I'd say just bust out the welder and griner and you'll have your 4-8 hp with out the $500 price tag.<P>-Rick||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||11-28-2001||12:59 AM||||The above is correct 4-8hp. But they look good, won't rust and won't crack. You can get more HP going with no cat and a Borla system. I think the total is 10-12hp.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Neal||11-28-2001||01:10 AM||||five fifty at the fierostore...<BR>for 550 just pony up the extra 50 and buy some REAL stainless headers from WCF, or SAVE 50 and buy their mild steel header.<P>It really does pain me to see those things installed on cars, no extra power over a 'fixed' stock manifold and at a rediculus price.||||reg||13
Z||000006||revin||11-28-2001||07:55 AM||||All I know is my sprint headers look nice.Easy to install. Sounds great. and more horses...well I got a hotter chip and free flowing cat.before I got the car started again(it was burned up). But it runs like and sounds like a rocket ship! Wiped a ricer off the road recently.<BR>As for porting.....no way! the stock manifolds are weak(thin)(part of the cause of the fire)the clogged cat was the other part of the fire. so MY opinion is opt for another type of manifold someone has them cheaper than F store.<P>------------------<BR>Revin||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||11-28-2001||08:05 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Neal:<BR><B>five fifty at the fierostore...<BR>for 550 just pony up the extra 50 and buy some REAL stainless headers from WCF, or SAVE 50 and buy their mild steel header.<P>It really does pain me to see those things installed on cars, no extra power over a 'fixed' stock manifold and at a rediculus price.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The WCF "shorty" headers are not Stainless, They are ceramic coated same as the Fiero Store Sprints. The WCF "Shorty" version has the same gains as the Sprints. The "shorty's" cost more once you add the ceramic coating. WCF does make a Full header set that runs close to $700 which is better and made out of stainless.<P>Kyle,<BR>Also mention you are a member of Pennock's and ask for the 10% discount. It will save you $50 more! <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||1FST2M6||11-28-2001||08:58 AM||||just a couple quick questions..<P>1) do you autocross<BR>2) is it a daily driver (traffic and such)<P>with sprint units or CW units you'll loose LOTS of low end torque. 8-15lbft! thats a decrease you CAN feel. you'll gain MAYBE 6-8hp above 4200..<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6headerdyno.jpg">  <P>unless your unnaturally aspirated, or always have your engine in the upper RPM range stick with stock units. (or if you've got 3.4)<BR>oh.. don't pay attention to the numbers.. those just show peak.. look at area under the curve... from 1500 to 4000 where you loose... <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fst2m6sig_1.gif">  <P> <A HREF="http://www.1fst2m6.com" TARGET=_blank>www.1fst2m6.com</A>  - underconstruction - but check it out anywho...<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||avengador1||11-28-2001||09:05 AM||||If you look at the dog bone replacement post you can see a picture of mine. I like the way they look and the fact that they don't take up much more room than the stock manifolds. They don't look as shinny after you run them for a while.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||lou_dias||11-28-2001||09:18 AM||||I had the sprints, a hollow cat and no muffler (IRM exhaust) with a crane 2030 cam and an overbored 3.4 and poorly ported (not polished) heads and intake and I made 203 ft*lbs. of torque.....  But hey, that's what 207 cubic inches is supposed to do right?||||reg||1
Z||000011||artherd||11-28-2001||10:15 PM||||Advantages:<BR>They won't crack. (they'll be the last time you mess with the exhaust, EVER!)<BR>slightly more hp (torque at speed) at the top, at the expense of slightly less torque down low.<BR>Sound cool<BR>Look bitchin.<P>Not *AT ALL* expensive at $550-600 for a full 3-piece header and y-pipe set. come on guys, this isn't a SBC, and you can't get these at Pep Boys for $49.95.<P>Disadvantages:<BR>$600 you couldda spent on a $1500 Held Motorsports 13" front brake kit. (or a v8, or...)<BR>+5 to 6bhp isn't a whole terrible lot. You'll feel it. barely. if you try really hard. and rev the piss out of a motor that likes to grenade above 5,000rpm...<P><BR>Basically, if I had a 'stock' Fiero that I wanted to keep *really really nice* then I'd go for them.  Also would go for them if I *EVER* had any thoughts of ever putting an OHV 3.4 in at a later time. (they'll give you much more with the 3.4)<P>Hope this helps, did I mention they look *FRIGGIN AWESOME* in your engine compartment? Jet-hot absolutely *rocks!*<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000012||avengador1||11-29-2001||07:09 PM||||For those that missed it here's mine. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero19_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
